{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgac7vAXkfaRExgmmPsL1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I proved `times_eq_mul` in `Main.lean`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\nThe proof works by induction on `n`:\n\n```lean\ntheorem times_eq_mul (n m : Nat) : times n m = n * m := by\n  induction n with\n  | zero => simp [times]\n  | succ k ih => simp [times, ih, Nat.succ_mul]\n```\n\n- **Base case:** `times 0 m` is `0` by definition, and `0 * m` simplifies to `0`.\n- **Inductive step:** `times (k+1) m` unfolds to `times k m + m`. The induction hypothesis turns that into `k * m + m`, and `Nat.succ_mul` rewrites `(k+1) * m` into that same form."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":7853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":443},"output_tokens":258,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2edfdb46-3dda-45a4-bf40-7dccccb4dfbd","uuid":"f5e99723-fa28-40cb-9e86-27fecc2fd415","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:10:04.008Z","request_id":"req_011Cgac7ug2BZFKwE3cKLEpL"}
